Choose **19-html-fragment** next. Its complete draft is 18 paragraphs, 91 Sentences, 17 InlineCode values and five External links, with no Sections, tables, lists, assets, foreign content, parallel variants or unresolved relative references. Its only legacy anchor is the article title. These structures are supported by the existing annotated `/2` and HTML page renderer; an explicit PageSet does not require a new resource registration for these external links. No production feature addition or manuscript shortening is justified by this preflight.

The source and draft match the archived independent content-review hashes exactly: source `1ef8b987603ce307f0622f3bb7ce19bdd8f7f94b78b34dfb8f8784e17e2022bf`, draft `373a519dffc1cbbc2bbd2b6334eef8d4490aae6c62798bf26918a5f280bfe083`. That content review was by a different agent; this reviewer originally authored 19, so today's reading is NOT a new independent semantic acceptance of its own manuscript. No unreflected source change was found. The original discussion of future shell/asset/operation work is preserved historical/specification scope, not an assertion that all such work remains unimplemented today.

