## Chapter 07: supported, with an extra anchor decision

07 has nine sibling Sections, 33 paragraphs, two nonadjacent flat lists (unordered five items; ordered start=1 six items), 11 unchecked ListItems each containing exactly one Paragraph. There are no links or assets. Paragraphs after a list are legal; no Body resumes ordinary content after a Section. There are no nested lists or unsupported table/foreign shapes. The source and draft hashes exactly match the previously integrated independent review: source `0005924591477574e490affa8df48d7446dfb41d81cd08beb55d03372a0dbfed`, draft `17618352d792b55cfa9436c029d1b5d09c916cc5af3b8123f4a33e053b963cae`.

The unchanged headings `6. NOR IR` and `7. SVG backend` contain no Ruby or Anno. Their future generated heading text is therefore unchanged, and the observed current GitHub automatic targets are exactly `6-nor-ir` and `7-svg-backend`. Blindly adding explicit aliases of both names risks the same name/id ambiguity previously observed in chapter 01. This is a concrete expected collision risk, NOT a newly executed failure against generated 07. Before cutover, explicitly choose and review the compatibility strategy (for example a meaningful author-approved heading clarification while retaining all old fragments and Section IDs); then verify actual generated GitHub DOM uniqueness. Do not silently remove a required fragment or add fake Japanese readings to unchanged Latin headings. This extra decision makes 19 the smaller immediate candidate.

