- `tools/src/doc/projection/annotated.rs:46` inspects the typed document and validates External URI spelling; other unresolved requirements remain failures. The five 19 targets match original Markdown in byte/order and are ASCII https links. No external resource was fetched to claim reachability or revision validity.
- `annotated.rs:248` traverses Sentence/Concat, Ruby and InlineCode and Link labels; `body:462` supports these paragraphs and Sections with explicit ordering restrictions. `annotated/blocks.rs:76` supports 07's exact flat-list shape. Ruby readings are retained in the all-notes view, not a Doc roundtrip encoding.
- Current `doc/canonical.json` contains five pages, neither candidate. Both candidates can use single-article `/2` for their own Markdown, even alongside the existing architecture page-context renderer. Canonical HTML still uses the real registered PageSet. Adding a page changes the explicit registry/context inputs; regenerate/check affected receipts and the full HTML set, rather than asserting old shared-budget results apply to six pages.
- Incoming human links in `doc/README.md` and inventory records retain the same `spec/07-circuit.md` / `spec/19-html-fragment.md` paths because these Markdown paths become generated entrypoints. This bounded search found no direct production tools/test dependency on those Markdown source files. It is not a whole-repository migration-reference audit. Do not delete historical inventory data or treat generated-entrypoint references as stale merely because the source format changes.

